https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZkQzP9D6vyg  (Capo 0)

TIP:  If transposing, play the root chord of the transposed (DaddA) and add the 5th note as necessary.

TIP:  The first part of the intro/outro is really meant to be picked, and it's pretty easy to do so, but can be strummed as well.  That (DaddA) is just (D) with your pinky stretched way over to the 5th fret.  You start there (holding (D) throughout), then slide (or lift and move) the pinky down to the 3rd fret for (Dsus4), lift off for (D) and repeat.  Then for the slide part it's one downstroke on the (D) and then a pause, one more downstroke and another pause, and then a quick two-count downstroke of (D).  This latter sequence repeats after the first chorus.

TIP:  There's one (Bm) in the chorus that'll catch you out if you're not ready for it. 
  

